{"text": "STEP 5 Position the drain hose The drain hose can be positioned in three ways: Over the edge of a wash basin The drain hose must be placed at a height of between 60 cm and 90 cm (*) from the floor. To keep the spout of the drain hose bent, use the supplied plastic hose guide (A). Secure the guide to the wall using a hook to ensure A stable drainage. In a drain pipe The drain pipe should be between 60 cm and 90 cm high (*). It is advisable to use a 65 cm high vertical pipe. \u2022 To ensure the drain hose stays in position, use the plastic hose guide provided (see the figure). \u2022 To prevent the siphoning of water flow during drainage, make sure to insert the drain hose 15 cm in the drain pipe. \u2022 To prevent the drain hose from moving around, secure the hose guide to the wall. Drain standpipe requirements: \u2022 Minimum diameter of 5 cm \u2022 Minimum carry-away capacity of 60 litres per minute English 25 WWWW55000000DD__IIBB__DD GGlloobbaall--PPJJTT__WWAASSHHEERR--MMDD__EENN((FFAA))..iinndddd 2255 22002255//44//2222 1100::3311::0088", "source": "D:\\Study\\4_Forth Semester\\AI\\project\\MultiAgent_RAG\\data\\Front_Load Washer AI Ecobuuble 9Kg_user_manual.pdf", "page": 24}